  <section class="lp-section lp-paper" id="methodology"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><h2>How we counted calls and meetings</h2></div>
    <div class="cc-report-method">
      <div id="fleet-source">
        <h3>Fleet repair records</h3>
        <p>CallTeam used its anonymized call log and meeting register for November 2–24, 2026. The campaign owner confirmed the new customer.</p>
        <p>The log counts each outbound call activity once. The 158 live conversations across 880 attempts give a 17.95% live conversation rate.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Other campaign results</h3>
        <p>The case studies document bookings and sales outcomes for the stated periods.</p>
        <p>The campaign team confirmed weekly call volumes, the SaaS and IT show rates, and the connection rates for September IT and MaxWell Realty Canada.</p>
        <p>For more on regions and call timing, see <a href="https://www.cognism.com/reports/cold-calling-report-2026">Cognism and WHAM’s 2026 cold calling report</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="lp-field-note cc-report-measurement" id="compare-your-campaign">
      <h3>How to compare your cold calling results</h3>
      <p>Use the same buyer group and dates for calls, conversations and bookings. For show rate, divide attended meetings by bookings due in that group. Count each rescheduled booking once.</p>
      <p>If few prospects answer, compare <a href="/resources/how-to-buy-cold-calling-leads/">direct and company numbers</a> for similar buyers. If people answer and seldom book, review your opener and qualifying question with the <a href="/cold-call-script-checker/">cold call script checker</a>.</p>
      <p>Check how many held meetings became opportunities with the <a href="/b2b-meeting-quality-check/">meeting quality check</a>. Use the <a href="/lead-generation-proposal-comparison/">proposal comparison tool</a> to see which agencies charge for booked, held or qualified meetings.</p>
      <a href="/articles/how-many-cold-calls-book-b2b-meeting/">Calculate how many calls you need per meeting</a>
    </div>
  </div></section>

